{"c":[{"id":"8d81c7b9a87754a7","sum":"B24, I3: person-details fill = 4 Jev calls (PER_FILL); Groq 429s, space writer calls 30 s; TextEdit opens files only from its Containers tmp; native <select> is a value-less hand-off; host memory.ndjson = helper golden, find lines by id.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d32f644355f794d8","sum":"B24: a person-details fill asks twice (whose, then values): 4 Jev calls, PER_FILL in counting tests; Groq qwen3.8 429s within ~20 plans, space writer calls 30 s; sandboxed TextEdit opens files only from its Containers tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-05aef102d22989aa","text":"B24: fill asks in two stages when a field takes a person's details (whose first, then values), so a fill is 4 Jev calls, not 2; tests that count calls use PER_FILL. Groq's qwen3.8 hits 429 token limits within ~20 plans; space writer calls 30 s.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T192504Z-2947a2d88b908a7e","text":"B24: TextEdit is sandboxed: a file named on its command line opens only from inside ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.TextEdit/Data/tmp (realfill-capture.ts makes its own folder there and deletes it).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e9b74ce9f7778aba","sum":"B24, I3: Chrome AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton with only the chosen option, so fill hands selects off with no value; host Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper golden byte for byte; tests find lines by id, never index.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-d09a0e8b1bd722e1","text":"B24: Chrome's AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton whose only child is the selected option; the option list is not readable without opening it, so fill names selects as hand-offs with no value (capture-2 probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195224Z-8ef6ab64ee3f2dea","text":"I3: apps/caret Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper's golden byte for byte as of H1 (host-memory-5 request added, A16's wrote line is host-memory-9, no -8); tests find lines by id, never by index.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3093b549fb68152a","sum":"I2-I3, W3: paste refused for unrestorable clipboard types; page-link snapshot mirrors Chrome AX; Helium reads NMH manifests from its --user-data-dir; page.sock proofs bind the helper pid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"787299ed8ad30f01","sum":"I2-I3: paste route refused when the prior clipboard holds a type outside restorableTypes (AX write, else clipboardUnrestorable); page-link toWindowSnapshot must mirror Chrome AX (AXTimeField, radios under an AXGroup per name, select options as AXMenuItem).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T195224Z-99ff86984f364892","text":"I3: host refuses the paste route when the prior clipboard holds a type outside ReconcilingClipboard.restorableTypes (file URL, private types): AX write instead, else fail clipboardUnrestorable. A17's VM probe lost a file-url item 5/5 while restore said restored.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195842Z-c30fb40a821e024f","text":"I2: page-link.ts toWindowSnapshot must match Chrome AX for fill/controls.ts: time is AXTimeField, radios sit under an AXGroup per name attribute, select options are AXMenuItem children. PageControl has no fieldset legend, so page radio groups have no label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"13ae7e710e2343cf","sum":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads NMH manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; both page.sock proofs (bridgeProof too) bind the helper pid, or a socket swap keeps the host's session.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-5a96910dba2d6b69","text":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads Native Messaging manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts (accept.ts --browser passes 42/42); its Web Store page offers Add to Helium.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-74ab7d13fad22cf2","text":"W3: page.sock proofs both bind the helper pid (bridgeProof too), or a same-user process that swaps the socket path can pass the host's hello to the real helper and keep that session.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
